<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wiz (200)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wiz &lt;text&gt;              (talk on the wizline)
wiz #&lt;level&gt; &lt;text&gt;     (only to gods of that level and up)
wiz @&lt;action&gt;           (an emote on the wizline; wiz @ &lt;action&gt; too)
wiz&#160;?                   (which gods are on)
wiz -                   (stop hearing the wizline)
wiz +                   (hear it again)
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>wiz Anyone know why the ferry is stuck?
wiz #245 The reboot is at midnight.
wiz @ waves to everyone.
</pre>
<p>The gods' own channel: every god in the game hears it, unless they have 
turned it off with wiz -. A line reads ":: Papi&#160;:: text"; with a level, 
":245: Papi&#160;:: text". While you are wizard-invisible above level 200, your 
lines go only to gods of your invisibility level and up. You can't limit 
it to a level above your own, and you can't talk on it while you are 
offline yourself.
</p><p>wiz&#160;? lists the gods in the game you can see, with their level, a * for 
those who are invisible, and a - for those who are offline.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wizinvisible</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Comm</a>
</pre>




</div>